**Known for**: Hashicorp (co-founder), Terraform, Vagrant, etc; Ghosttty; Superlogical

Mitchell is the wealthy co-founder of Hashicorp and is currently in vogue for
his vibe-coded terminal emulator Ghostty, and has many personal and financial
relationships with rich weird little guys.

Mitchell is on the board of directors at Vercel, where [Guillermo Rauch][rauch]
is CEO.[[source]][0] Guilleremo is also an investor in Mitchell's latest
venture, Superlogical, where Mitchell works with associates and alumni of
Hashicorp, Vercel, and Shopify.[[source]][1]

Other investors in Superlogical include [Tobias Lütke][lutke], CEO of Shopify,
as well as various sponsors of [David Heinemeier Hansson][dhh]'s Omarchy
project, including Patrick Collision, CEO of Stripe. Paul Coppelstone, CEO of
Supabase, also sponsors both Superlogical and [Andreas Kling][kling]'s Ladybird
project. Mitchell is an associate of David Heinemeier
Hansson,[[source]][2][[source]][3] and he uses and regularly promotes
Omarchy.[[source]][4]

